gdbm: Declare fatal error callback parameter

The fatal error callback is invoked with a char pointer, but its declarations
use an empty parameter list. With C23 semantics this declares a function that
takes no arguments and causes compilation to fail. Declare the callback
parameter consistently in the implementation, public header, and manuals.

Upstream-Status: Pending

